integrating her into ash which i  think is a bit weird since the undead  lady from episode one didn't  disintegrate when she was stabbed in the  heart  so whatever Zoe asked Jack to leave  which she says is for Dracula's own good  but I think it's really because she  knows she needs to sacrifice herself in  order for Dracula to be killed once and  for all with Zoe and Dracula alone she  rips the curtains off exposing Dracula  to daylight but he survives he's not  affected by sunlight at all and Zoe  knows it everything Dracula had been  afraid of they cross the sunlight going  into homes without being invited were  simply habits he had picked up over the  years and believed to be true Zoe needs  to expose this to get at the root of  what Dracula is really afraid of death  everyone in Dracula's family died a  courageous ro of death on the  battlefield while he sculpt about in the  shadows of the castle he became afraid  of death and ironically fell in love  with  girl who didn't fear death at all Lucy  that's what made her so attractive to  him and why he fed on her over and over  his fear of the cross stems from the  fact it represents the courage he longs  to possess the courage it takes to die  Zoe is the antithesis of Dracula ready  to die in the face of the cancer that  has taken over her body the only way to  conquer death she says is to face it  without fear until Dracula is dead she  says to him we live forever  with this realization Dracula approaches  the window in one of my favorite shots  of the entire series his body wrapped in  sunlight with the shadow of the Cross  reflecting onto it two things that he  lived in fear of he's now embracing the  only thing left is death as the screen  fades to white we transition to the  Streamlight state of him making love to  Agatha but in reality he's drinking  Agatha's poisonous blood he knows that  it will kill him and in the process also  kill her he has embraced death and let  go of fear walking away from an eternal  life of shame the final shot is of these  two arch-nemesis together as one in bed  as we fade to a picture of the Sun the  thing he once feared but now calls  beautiful Dracula may not be the most  original interpretation of the Brahm  Stoker novel but overall I found it to  be a fun cat-and-mouse game between  sister Agatha and Dracula but I want to  hear what you thought of the show below  make sure to give the video a like and  subscribe as 20:20 will be filled with  new episode breakdowns and they explain  videos and tons of other surprises until  next time remember love life
 

